## Summary

I've created comprehensive tests for `repairBuilding` in `/Users/tijs/projects/local-model-bench/runner/runs/tmph46gmget/run/tests/repair.test.ts` with 13 test cases covering all required behaviors:

**Repairs a building for half its cost (rounded up):**
- Repairs a hut with even cost (10 → 5 wood)
- Repairs a farm with odd costs that round up (15 wood → 8, 5 stone → 3)
- Repairs a quarry with even cost (20 → 10 wood)

**Is a no-op if building doesn't exist:**
- Returns unchanged settlement when requesting to repair a building the settlement doesn't have
- Returns unchanged settlement when settlement has no buildings

**Never takes resources below 0:**
- Clamps to 0 when wood insufficient (3 available vs 5 needed)
- Clamps to 0 when stone insufficient (2 available vs 3 needed)
- Clamps to 0 when repair cost greatly exceeds available resources
- Handles already-zero resources without going negative

**Multiple buildings & rounding:**
- Only repairs the specified building when settlement has multiple
- Repairs same building type appearing multiple times (uses `includes()`)
- Verifies odd cost rounding (5/2 = 3)
- Handles insufficient resources with odd costs

